 Flutter overflow playbook (what we learned)

 Bound things: give content a max width/height when needed (ConstrainedBox/SizedBox).

 Dialogs specifically: AlertDialog uses intrinsic sizing → don’t put LayoutBuilder inside. Use
 ConstrainedBox(maxWidth: ~520) → SingleChildScrollView → Column(mainAxisSize: min).

 Horizontal controls: long rows (e.g. ToggleButtons / action bars)

 drop fixed minWidth

 wrap in SizedBox(height: 40) + SingleChildScrollView(scrollDirection: Axis.horizontal)

 shorten labels on narrow screens; let text ellipsis.

 Expanded/Flexible: avoid inside a Column that lives in a scroll view (unbounded height). Only use them when the axis is bounded.

 If still tight: switch rows to Wrap, reduce paddings, or show icon-only variants.

